            <div xml:id="d1000">

                <pb facs="0671" n="599" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg599"/>

                <head>Government of the Canton of Unterwalden Lower</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanz</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-04">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 4, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Council of Lower Unterwalden to the honorable
                        Bundesrath, in Berne</hi>.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: Following the example of the Union
                    Council and the governments of several cantons, allow us to express our deepest
                    sympathy for the American Union. It is a great honor for the Swiss people, at a
                    time when great grief has overwhelmed the sister republic of America, not to
                    remain dumb, but to speak out their sympathy for the cause of social
                    freedom.</p>
                <p>We therefore enclose our address of sympathy, and beg you will send it, with the
                    others, to its proper destination.</p>
                <p>We recommend you to protecting Providence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>LWYRSOH, <hi rendition="#italic">President</hi>.</item>
                            <item>A. WAGNER, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
